# What the build context must not carry.
#
# docker/Dockerfile names every COPY path explicitly, so this file is not the only
# thing keeping junk out of the image -- but the daemon transfers the whole context
# before the first COPY runs, and .venv alone is larger than the image. The entries
# below are also the guarantee behind AC8: nothing here can reach /app even if a
# later ticket adds a broader COPY.

# Git metadata: an image that shipped .git would ship every prior revision of the
# source it was built from.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# The host virtualenv. The image builds its own with `uv sync --frozen`; copying
# the host's would put macOS/arm64 wheels into a linux image.
.venv

# Implementation-loop working state: change plans, gate receipts, logs.
.loop

# S3 working directories, not sources of truth. The Dockerfile mkdirs /app/artifacts
# itself, and models/ is staged output on its way to storage.model_uri_prefix.
artifacts
models

# dbt build output and vendored packages; `dbt deps` regenerates them in-container.
dbt/target
dbt/dbt_packages
dbt/logs
dbt/profiles/.user.yml

# Caches, byte-code and editor droppings.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation and agent tooling: neither is read at runtime.
docs
.claude
.github
